sanctioned: this program exercises the new accessor-typed Store query leaves (neq, gt, gte, lt, lte, like, inList, inListBy) on a typed record store built from a hand-assembled Codec Item with SRecord shape. Ipe.Db.Store is an Ipê-only addition with no counterpart in the reference backend, and Ipê emits Rust+sqlx while the reference emits a different backend, so a shared Main.ipe cannot run on both. Ipê's output is recorded as the correct reference. The eight output lines count rows matching each leaf: (1) gt .qty 9 — 1 row (widget:30); (2) lt .qty 10 — 2 rows (gizmo:9, sprocket:5); (3) gte .qty 9 — 2 rows (widget:30, gizmo:9); (4) lte .qty 9 — 2 rows (gizmo:9, sprocket:5); (5) neq .name "widget" — 2 rows; (6) like .name "w%" — 1 row (widget); (7) inList .qty [30, 9] — 2 rows; (8) inListBy Codec.string .name ["widget"] — 1 row. Every value binds as a positional SQL parameter, never spliced into the query string.
